# FIELD-WINTER: FIELD_Barn_Winter = FIELD_Barn under the world's snow layer (Common/WeatherSnow.glslh): the scene's
# collection WP_Winter names the CC0 ambientCG Snow010A albedo / normal / ARM as Texture world parameters and
# SnowCover 0.9; the look is the scan, the code only places it by the up-facing normal (owner 10-29).
Дано run Scene "Open Scene FIELD_Barn_Winter.desce"
Дано run View "View mode: Lit"
Дано run Entity "Sun"
Дано --subject selection set SunElevation 25
Дано --subject selection set SunAzimuth 110
Дано --subject viewport set Camera.Position 0,170,2500
Дано --subject viewport set Camera.Direction 0.15,-0.25,-1
Тогда-вид 1_winter_eye ground, barn roof and branches carry the scanned snow (grain, sparkle-free white, soft relief) on up-facing faces; walls and trunks stay bare; blades poke out of the snow; the ground under the grass is not black; editor.log errors 0
Когда --subject viewport set Camera.Position 0,900,2500
Когда --subject viewport set Camera.Direction 0.15,-0.15,-1
Тогда-вид 2_winter_high the whole field white under snow to the horizon, the far landscape beyond the crest (Terrain Far) included, no sharp snow edge at grazing distance, no tiling grid visible at 9 m, roof white, wall faces dark and bare, no black patches
